 matrix 4 that he has  met with kevin feige to talk about roles  in the mcu but they have not agreed on a  role yet they haven't found a role that  would be perfect for keanu reeves yet so  it's not keanu reeves but good news for  the walking dead fans it could be norman  reedus most people know him as daryl  from the walking dead and there's a  little bit of evidence suggesting that  he could have already been cast as the  mcu's ghostwriter let's take a look at  it now according to charles murphy of  murphy's multiverse.com an actor has  indeed been chosen to play ghostwriter  with this news comes a lot of reports  that norman reedus has been chosen to  play ghostwriter and what's very  interesting about this is that norman  reedus has been liking the tweets tweets  about him himself playing ghostwriter  and tweets just about ghostwriter being  cast in general he's liked several  tweets so far about ghostwriter and to  top it all off on twitter he tweeted a  link to an instagram page that had fan  art of him as ghost rider which is a  pretty big sign so either he's the  greatest troll of all time or there is  actually a decent chance that he has  indeed been cast as johnny blaise aka  ghost writer in the mcu assuming they go  with johnny blaze of course now as far  as when we can expect to see ghost rider  in the mcu all signs right now kind of  point towards doctor strange and the  multiverse of madness we've heard rumors  for over a year now that ghost rider  will be making his mcu debut in  multiverse of madness and at the time we  didn't know if it was going to be an  older ghost writer a variant of ghost  rider or if we would be getting our mcu  ghostwriter in the film and it looks  like it could be our very own  ghostwriter and the timing of this kind  of checks out doctor strange is  supposedly going to introduce many  different new aspects of the mcu one of  those aspects is a darker side to the  mcu remember this movie was originally  supposed to be a horror film scott  derrickson was originally supposed to  direct the film he wanted it to be a  true horror film and what we've heard is  that kevin feige said no it's still  gotta be pg-13 it can't be that much of  a horror film they kind of disagreed  about the vision so they parted ways and  now sam raimi is stepping up who of  course has a horror background and he is  directing multiverse of madness so it's  not going to be all out not going to be  just a true full-on horror film which  i'm excited about i don't really do  horror that well but based off of what  we know it is going to be pretty trippy  and it's going to be dark and introduce  the supernatural side of the mcu such as  dark magic demons and of course we'll  probably explore the dark hold a little  bit more as well which in the comics was  created by an ancient evil elder god  c'thun and like i said a lot of new  things are going to be introduced in  this film and one of those things or i  should say groups is supposedly going to  be some type of a setup for the midnight  suns not sure if they'll all come  together in this film but the setup for  them should happen in multiverse of  madness ghost rider of course is a part  of the midnight suns group and then we  have blade coming to the mcu we've  actually kind of already seen his mcu  debut in the post-credits scene for the  eternals spoiler alert if you haven't  seen it with kid harrington but kit  harrington's dane whitman aka the black  knight is about to pick up the sword and  right before he picks up the sword we  hear a voice ask him if he's sure he  wants to do that it has been confirmed  that this is the voice of mahershala ali  aka the actor who is playing blade in  the mcu so blade has already been  introduced then of course doctor strange  himself is a part of the midnight suns  and then the other big name who is a  part of the midnight suns is the  punisher and i'm not trying to get  anybody's hopes up this is my own  speculation but they 